loss":"Tamil land"},{"surface":"கேட்ப","parts":[{"text":"கேட்ப","lemma":"கேட்ப","gloss":"to hear"}],"gloss":"to hear","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொய்யா","parts":[{"text":"பொய்","lemma":"poy","gloss":"lie"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"negative relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"unfailing"},{"surface":"செந்நா","parts":[{"text":"செந்நா","lemma":"செந்நா","gloss":"truthful tongue"}],"gloss":"truthful tongue","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நெளிய","parts":[{"text":"நெளி","lemma":"neḷi","gloss":"bend/move"},{"text":"ய","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to bend"},{"surface":"ஏத்தி","parts":[{"text":"ஏத்து","lemma":"ēttu","gloss":"praise"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"absolutive suffix"}],"gloss":"praising"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடுப","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"sing"},{"text":"உப","lemma":"upa","gloss":"habitual future plural suffix"}],"gloss":"they will sing"},{"surface":"என்ப","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"say"},{"text":"ப","lemma":"pa","gloss":"plural suffix"}],"gloss":"they say"},{"surface":"பரிசிலர்","parts":[{"text":"பரிசிலர்","lemma":"paricilar","gloss":"supplicants"}],"gloss":"supplicants"},{"surface":"நாளும்","parts":[{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"nāḷ","gloss":"day"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even/always"}],"gloss":"daily"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஈயா","parts":[{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ī","gloss":"give"},{"text":"யா","lemma":"ā","gloss":"negative relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"ungiving"},{"surface":"மன்னர்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னர்","lemma":"maṉṉar","gloss":"kings"}],"gloss":"kings"},{"surface":"நாண","parts":[{"text":"நாண்","lemma":"nāṇ","gloss":"be ashamed"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to be ashamed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வீயாது","parts":[{"text":"வீ","lemma":"vī","gloss":"perish"},{"text":"யாது","lemma":"ātu","gloss":"negative absolutive suffix"}],"gloss":"without perishing"},{"surface":"பரந்த","parts":[{"text":"பர","lemma":"para","gloss":"spread"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"n","gloss":"euphonic glide"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"spread"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"வசை","parts":[{"text":"வசை","lemma":"vacai","gloss":"fault/blame"}],"gloss":"fault"},{"surface":"இல்","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"il","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"less"},{"surface":"வான்","parts":[{"text":"வான்","lemma":"vāṉ","gloss":"great/sky"}],"gloss":"great"},{"surface":"புகழே","parts":[{"text":"புகழ்","lemma":"pukaḻ","gloss":"fame"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"fame indeed"}]}],"literal":"Waterfall roaring bamboo-dense wide-space / black-pepper-growing mountain-slope blossomed gloriosa-lily / fat tuber to-be-uprooted digging with-kin / fierce-eyed wild-boar plowed dust / good day coming-season looking-at hill-dwellers / without-plowing sowed thick-eared small millet / early-ripening new-yield day-freshness to-eat / wild-cow milked foam-bearing sweet milk / deer-meat cooked flesh-smelling pot / bright-colored iron-side without-washing placing-on-fire / sandalwood firewood-with boiled millet-rice / kūtaḷam-flowers beautified wild-jasmine front-yard / fertile-bunch banana broad-leaf distributing / unridden horse lord sharp-spear / fragrant-fiber tied kino-flower garland / beauty-practiced arrow bowmen chief / hand-generous giving swift-horse Koṟṟa / earth boundary Tamil-land to-hear / unfailing truthful-tongue to-bend praising / will-sing they-say supplicants daily / ungiving kings to-be-ashamed / without-perishing spread your faultless great fame","translation":"In the wide mountain slopes where waterfalls roar and bamboos grow dense, wild boars with fierce eyes dig up the fat tubers of blossomed gloriosa lilies on the pepper-growing slopes, leaving the soil plowed. Watching for the auspicious season, the hill-dwellers sow thick-eared small millet without plowing. To eat the early-ripening fresh yield, they cook the millet rice on a fire of sandalwood logs in a soot-blackened iron pot, unwashed, in which deer meat had been cooked and sweet, foamy milk of wild cows had been boiled. In the front yard beautified by wild jasmine and kūtaḷam flowers, they distribute this food on broad banana leaves. O Koṟṟa, lord of unridden horses, bearer of a sharp spear, chief of bowmen with well-crafted arrows, wearing a garland of kino flowers tied with fragrant fibers, and known for your swift horses and generous hands! Supplicants praise you daily with truthful tongues that never lie, so that the whole Tamil land within the boundaries of this earth hears it, making ungenerous kings feel ashamed, as your faultless, great fame spreads endlessly.","modern":"அருவிகள் முழங்கும் மூங்கில்கள் நிறைந்த அகன்ற மலைப்பகுதியில், மிளகு வளரும் சரிவுகளில் மலர்ந்த காந்தள் மலரின் கொழுத்த கிழங்குகளைக் கிளைகளோடு காட்டுப்பன்றிகள் தோண்டி உழுதன. அந்தப் புழுதியில், நல்ல நாளைப் பார்த்து மலைவாழ் குறவர்கள் உழாமலேயே பருத்த கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட தினையை விதைத்தனர். அவ்வாறு விளைந்த புதிய தினையரிசியை, காட்டுப் பசுவின் நுரை பொங்கும் இனிமையான பாலையும் மான்கறியையும் சமைத்த கரிய பானையைக் கழுவாமல் அப்படியே ஏற்றி, சந்தனக் கட்டைகளை விறகாகக் கொண்டு சமைத்தனர். காட்டு மல்லிகையும் கூதளமும் அழகு செய்யும் முற்றத்தில், செழுமையான வாழை இலையில் அந்த உணவைப் பகிர்ந்து உண்பர். அடக்க முடியாத குதிரைகளை உடையவனே! கூர்மையான வேலையும், கூர் வடித்த அம்புகளையும் வில்லையும் உடைய வீரர்களின் தலைவனே! வாரி வழங்கும் வள்ளல் தன்மையும் வேகமான குதிரைகளையும் கொண்ட கொற்றனே! உலக எல்லையில் உள்ள தமிழகம் முழுவதும் கேட்கும்படி, பொய் கூறாத நாக்கினைக் கொண்ட பரிசிலர்கள் உன்னைப் புகழ்ந்து பாடுகின்றனர். இதனால் கொடை தராத பிற மன்னர்கள் நாணமடையும்படி, உன்னுடைய குற்றமற்ற பெரும் புகழ் அழியாமல் எங்கும் பரவியுள்ளது.","explanation":"This poem is addressed to the chieftain Piṭṭaṅ Koṟṟaṉ by the poet Karuvūr Kanthappiḷḷai Sāthanār in the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai. The poet praises the chieftain's immense generosity and valor by describing the rich, fertile mountain country he rules. The imagery of the hill-dwellers (kuṟavar) cooking fresh millet in unwashed pots that previously held rich milk and deer meat, using precious sandalwood as firewood, highlights the natural abundance and hospitality of his land. The wild boars digging up gloriosa lily tubers act as natural plows, showing how even nature works to sustain the people without hard labor. The poet contrasts Koṟṟaṉ's boundless giving with other ungenerous kings who are put to shame by his widespread, faultless fame. Key words include 'ஈகை' (generosity), 'கொற்ற' (Koṟṟaṉ), and 'புகழ்' (fame).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,1.5],[1.5,2.1],[2.1,2.6],[2.6,3.2],[3.2,4.1],[4.1,4.57],[4.57,5.4],[5.4,5.6],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,6.3],[6.3,6.92],[6.92,7.3],[7.3,7.7],[7.7,8.0],[8.0,9.1],[9.1,9.5],[9.5,9.9],[9.9,10.3],[10.3,11.2],[11.2,11.56],[11.56,12.2],[12.2,12.5],[12.5,13.89],[13.89,14.03],[14.1,14.9],[14.9,15.2],[15.2,16.2],[16.2,16.5],[16.5,16.7],[16.7,17.5],[18.24,18.6],[18.6,19.04],[19.04,19.74],[19.74,20.14],[20.14,21.34],[21.34,21.84],[22.14,22.34],[22.34,22.81],[22.81,23.17],[23.17,23.64],[23.64,24.24],[24.24,24.58],[24.58,25.31],[25.31,26.04],[26.04,26.24],[26.24,26.54],[26.54,27.37],[27.37,27.79],[27.79,28.47],[28.47,29.04],[29.04,29.84],[29.84,30.34],[30.34,30.64],[30.64,31.04],[31.04,31.74],[31.82,32.22],[32.22,32.64],[32.64,32.87],[32.87,33.04],[33.04,34.44],[34.44,34.64],[34.64,35.04],[35.8,36.2],[36.4,36.6],[36.6,37.0],[37.0,37.2],[37.2,37.5],[37.5,38.0],[38.0,38.4],[38.4,39.2],[39.2,40.1],[40.1,40.3],[40.3,40.5],[40.5,40.9],[40.9,41.35],[41.35,41.8],[41.8,42.2],[42.2,42.8],[43.17,43.9],[43.9,44.3],[44.4,44.88],[44.88,45.6],[45.6,46.0],[46.0,46.4],[46.4,46.6],[46.6,47.1]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.9],[0.9,1.6],[1.6,2.3],[2.3,3.4],[3.4,3.6],[3.6,4.7],[4.7,4.9],[4.9,6.1],[6.1,6.6],[6.6,7.1],[7.1,7.5],[7.5,8.25],[8.25,8.7],[8.7,9.3],[9.3,9.7],[9.7,10.35],[10.35,11.15],[11.15